# Allowlist for the jscpd copy/paste gate (`cargo xtask check-jscpd`, issue #474).
#
# One audited clone per non-comment line. The format is
#
#   <relative-path>:<start-line> == <relative-path>:<start-line> : <reason>
#
# where the two fragments are the clone's files and 1-based start lines (as jscpd reports
# them, relative to the repo root), and the reason after the ` : ` is the ONLY thing a
# reviewer reads to decide whether the exemption is still earned. Matching is on both
# fragments' `path:start`, in either order, so transposing the two files grants the same
# clone.
#
# An intentional clone belongs here with a reason; loosening the gate's thresholds is not an
# allowlist. The tree below starts EMPTY - there are no excused clones - so an entry appearing
# here is a visible, reviewed decision rather than a way to silence a red build. A line that
# names a clone the gate no longer finds is inert (like a `[warn]` entry under the line cap in
# `devco/max-lines-ignore`) and should be deleted with its reason when the clone it excused
# leaves the tree.

# No entries. A deliberate clone is added here with its reason.
